      "title": "Container images must not use forbidden reference (pinned by digest)",
      "desc": "A container image in the pipeline uses a tag that is forbidden by the configuration (e.g., 'latest', 'dev'). Mutable tags make builds non-reproducible because the underlying image can change without notice.",
      "types": [
        "CI/CD Security",
        "Supply Chain",
        "Security"
      ],
      "src_url": "https://getplumber.io/docs/cli/issues/ISSUE-102"
    },
    "remediation": {
      "desc": "Pin the image to a specific immutable version tag (e.g., 'python:3.12.1' instead of 'python:latest'). Configure forbidden tags in .plumber.yaml under containerImageMustNotUseForbiddenTags.tags. Pin the image using its digest: 'image: registry.example.com/myimage@sha256:abc123...'. You can find the digest with 'docker inspect --format={{.RepoDigests}} \u003cimage\u003e'."
    },
