      "name": "Forbidden container image tag",
      "message": "Job `build` uses the forbidden tag `latest` of image `docker.io/node:latest`.",
      "description": "A container image in the pipeline uses a tag that is forbidden by the configuration (e.g., 'latest', 'dev'). Mutable tags make builds non-reproducible because the underlying image can change without notice.\n\nFinding: Job `build` uses the forbidden tag `latest` of image `docker.io/node:latest`.\n\nA new version of `docker.io/node:latest` runs inside `build` without any change in this repository, holding secrets Plumber could not list: code runs on an ephemeral runner and nothing else is proven.",
      "severity": "Low",
      "solution": "Pin the image to a specific immutable version tag (e.g., 'python:3.12.1' instead of 'python:latest'). Configure forbidden tags in .plumber.yaml under containerImageMustNotUseForbiddenTags.tags.",
